---
// FAQPage JSON-LD schema — injected into the head of FAQ page
---
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is LocalCloud?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "LocalCloud is a local Google Cloud runtime that brings the major Google Cloud services teams reach for first into a single Docker container. It gives you one boot path, one localhost handoff for SDKs, and a built-in console for inspecting the runtime locally."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is LocalCloud free?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes — LocalCloud is free for individual developers for evaluation, personal projects, learning, and testing. It is not licensed for commercial or production use."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is LocalCloud different from individual Google emulators?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Google provides some emulator paths, but you still have to run and manage them separately. LocalCloud wraps the major services developers need into one container."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need to change my application code to use LocalCloud?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. LocalCloud works with standard GCP SDK and CLI clients. You only change environment variables to point service endpoints at localhost."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which SDK languages are supported?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Any language with GCP SDK support works: Python, Node.js, Go, Java, C#, Ruby, PHP, and more."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How complete is the BigQuery emulation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The BigQuery emulator provides ~96% SQL coverage, 818 functional tests, 200+ mapped functions and features."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use LocalCloud in CI/CD?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. LocalCloud runs in any environment with Docker support. Add it as a service in your CI pipeline."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much memory does LocalCloud need?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Recommended: 4GB. With fewer services enabled, 2GB may suffice."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does LocalCloud take to start?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The default boot path is designed to come up in less than 1 minute on a typical development machine."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is data persisted between restarts?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, if you mount a Docker volume to /var/lib/localcloud. Without a volume, data is lost when the container stops."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
